18
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:38,760
Um this is more general interest, I guess, than news, but uh Bill Pugh, who is the uh teacher who uh had a hand in rewriting the new state standards for communication technologies in the state of Florida, uh having holography written into that for next school year, uh came up to Allentown to visit the studio and uh do some work, and we took a few of his laser pointers and his laser diodes and put them on the table.

19
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:46,920
He was having uh difficulty giving getting images uh and we wanted to test to see what the trouble was.

20
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:51,960
So among the a number of other things that he was up here for as well.

21
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:58,440
So we uh took the laser diodes and I set up an interferometer and I found something very, very interesting.

22
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:15,720
And uh he had an infinitor, which is what Steve Michael and I have been using for uh quite some time to create the laser diode holograms or laser pointer holograms, and uh that showed a real nice uh pattern of uh fringes.

23
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,960
Uh not very stable.

24
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:34,440
I mean, there were times when it was stable, but every so often it would sort of like uh throw a little bit of a fit and the fringes would move or they'd go away or do this and that, and it happened every so often, you know, the fringes would come back in and seemed really nice, and then it would happen again that you know they'd start to drift.

25
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:40,920
But you know for 1499, that's certainly to be expected.

26
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:50,480
What was really interesting is he o also ordered a few other laser pointers or laser diodes, however you want to term them.

27
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:54,640
Uh one of them was for a gun sight on a gun.

28
00:03:54,640 --> 00:04:00,080
Obviously that's why it's called a gun sight, uh for a handheld gun.

29
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:05,920
And he said he was not able to ever get a successful hologram using this gun sight.

30
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:10,720
So, you know, I reviewed the material and it looked like a very nice uh setup.

31
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:18,800
Um had a 635 nanometer diode uh colonnading lens and provided a beautiful beam.

32
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:27,280
I mean, this beam looked cleaner than any helium neon laser beam I've uh ever seen come out of a tube.

33
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:44,080
And uh very sharp and uh uh very nice looking beam, which you would think that this would be able to create holograms, but I put it on the interferometer, and would you believe we could not even get fringes?

34
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,600
Nothing.

35
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:48,160
It was that bad.

36
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:53,760
He also had a I guess you would call it a module.

37
00:04:53,760 --> 00:05:07,600
It was uh the laser diode in housing, and it also had the chip sticking out of the back of the laser diode housing with two pigtail wires coming off of it that you connected your battery to.

38
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,360
And we put that up there as well.

39
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:19,360
Uh, I don't know if he tested, I can't really remember from the other day whether he said he tested his making holograms and wasn't successful with it or not, or whether he even used it at all.

40
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:26,320
But uh once again I put it on the interferometer, and there were fringes, but they were very light gray.

41
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:32,120
In fact, if you didn't know what to look for, you wouldn't have seen or noticed the fringes at all.

42
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:44,360
Which leads us to believe that it's not always possible to use anything when it comes to these uh diodes and diode modules to make holograms.

43
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:48,280
And you know, we're gonna have to find out what you can use and what you can't use.

44
00:05:48,280 --> 00:06:06,040
If someone all of a sudden decided that they wanted to order that gun site and try to make holograms with it, they'd be completely out of luck because no matter how hard I tried, we could not even get any fringes at all with the laser light.

45
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:13,960
Now I don't know whether this has anything to do with the uh drive circuit or whether it's the diode.

46
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:19,720
I imagine the 635 nanometer diode is going to be a 635 nanometer diode.

47
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:32,120
My guess, and this is just from working with them to begin with and my guess is as good as anyone else is out there on this as far as this goes, is that uh the answer basically is in the drive circuitry.

48
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:45,160
I don't think I I think you could probably take one of those diodes and just hook it up to a more accurate power supply driver and all of a sudden you'd notice that you have fringes.

49
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:57,320
This may be true, this may not be true, but that's the feeling that I get and um it's very important if you're deciding to start with uh laser diode holography that uh you'd be very careful in what you buy.

50
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:00,920
Now we do know the infinitors work very well for fourteen ninety nine.

51
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:07,800
I think you paid a pretty hefty price for this gun site, and it turns out it's not capable of making a hologram at all.

52
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:11,600
Very interesting, but I think a lot of this has to do with the drive circuit.

53
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,960
And it's quite possible.

54
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:24,240
Now I know when I was reading the instructions it said that it actually had a an adjustable potentiometer on there, uh adjustable resistor, uh, where you could uh turn down the drive current.

55
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:33,520
Um I really should have turned that down a little bit and you know seen if that helped because it may be overdriving it.

56
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:39,040
Uh in order for it to be a gun site and uh cover as much distance as possible.

57
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:50,800
It uh they may actually have that uh uh variable resistor set so high that fringes fringes are are just destroyed when you put it onto a uh interferometer.

58
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,960
It's just it's just over driving too much.

59
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:58,640
So that that may be the problem right there, but uh who wants to go through all that trouble.

60
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:10,320
